# AGENTS.md — `lab/`

Root [`../AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) applies. This directory describes the
physical world, which an agent cannot observe.

## Non-negotiable local constraint

Do not fabricate or infer protocol execution, sample identity, reagent lot,
measurement, observation, date, deviation, operator, or ELN link. Missing facts
stay visibly missing until a person or authoritative record supplies them.

## Allowed assistance

- Reformat user-provided facts without changing meaning.
- Draft a reusable protocol template clearly marked as unexecuted.
- Check supplied bench records against `metadata/` and report discrepancies
  without silently correcting either side.
- Maintain stable pointers after the user identifies the authoritative record.

{% if bench_record_authority == "eln" -%}
The ELN is authoritative for executed facts.
{% if bench_record_location %}Use only the configured location
`{{ bench_record_location }}`; do not broaden or substitute scope.
{% else %}Its location is unconfigured. Ask the user; do not guess or create a
repository fallback.
{% endif %}

Do not create executed records under `lab/records/` in ELN mode.
{% else -%}
Repository record mode is active. A person must supply/approve executed facts in
`lab/records/`. Agents may format those facts but may not create the scientific
content or certify completeness.
{% endif -%}
